"2549","Al-Silsila-tu-Ahadees-e-Sahiha Hadees: 2549 Arabic Hadees: 3050"
"2550","Al-Silsila-tu-Ahadees-e-Sahiha Hadees: 2550 Arabic Hadees: 3237"
"2551","Al-Silsila-tu-Ahadees-e-Sahiha Hadees: 2551 Arabic Hadees: 3077"
"2552","Al-Silsila-tu-Ahadees-e-Sahiha Hadees: 2552 Arabic Hadees: 2064"
"2553","Abdur-Rahman bin Abd Rabb al-Ka'bah said: I entered the mosque and found Abdullah bin Amr bin al-As sitting in the shade of the Ka'bah, with people gathered around him. I came to them and sat with him. He said: We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on a journey, so we alighted at a stopping place. Some of us were setting up their tents, some were shooting arrows, and some were tending to their beasts. Then the caller of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ announced: ""Prayer is a gathering."" So we gathered around the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said: ""There was no prophet before me but it was incumbent upon him to guide his nation to the best of what he knew for them and to warn them against the worst of what he knew for them. And your nation, its well-being has been placed in its first part, and its last part will be afflicted with calamities and things you will deny. A trial (fitnah) will come, making some of it follow others. A trial will come and the believer will say: 'This is my destruction.' Then it will be lifted. A trial will come and the believer will say: 'This is it, this is it.' So whoever wishes to be removed from the Fire and admitted into Paradise, let death come to him while he believes in Allah and the Last Day, and let him treat people as he would love to be treated. And whoever pledges allegiance to an Imam, giving him the clasp of his hand and the fruit of his heart, let him obey him as long as he is able. If another comes to dispute with him, strike the neck of the other.""He added at the end: I drew close to him and said to him: ""I adjure you by Allah, did you hear this from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?"" He pointed to his ears and his heart with his hands and said: ""My ears heard it and my heart retained it."" I said to him: ""This cousin of yours, Mu'awiyah, orders us to consume our wealth among ourselves unjustly and to kill ourselves, while Allah says: [And do not consume one another's wealth unjustly... and do not kill yourselves...] (An-Nisa)."" He remained silent for a while, then said: ""Obey him in obedience to Allah, and disobey him in disobedience to Allah."""
"2554","Al-Silsila-tu-Ahadees-e-Sahiha Hadees: 2554 Arabic Hadees: 918"
"2555","Al-Silsila-tu-Ahadees-e-Sahiha Hadees: 2555 Arabic Hadees: 770"
"2556","Al-Silsila-tu-Ahadees-e-Sahiha Hadees: 2556 Arabic Hadees: 3257"
"2557","From Al-Aswad ibn Yazid, who said: The prayer was established in the mosque, so we came walking with Abdullah ibn Mas'ud. When the people bowed, Abdullah bowed and we bowed with him while still walking. A man passed in front of him and said: ""Peace be upon you, O Abu Abdur-Rahman!"" Abdullah said while bowing: ""Allah and His Messenger have spoken the truth."" When he finished the prayer, some of the people asked him: ""Why did you say, when the man greeted you, 'Allah and His Messenger have spoken the truth'?"" He said: ""I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) say: 'Indeed, among the portents of the Hour is that the greeting is given only on the basis of acquaintance.' In another narration: 'That a man greets a man only because of acquaintance.'"""
"2558","Al-Silsila-tu-Ahadees-e-Sahiha Hadees: 2558 Arabic Hadees: 2272"
"2559","Al-Silsila-tu-Ahadees-e-Sahiha Hadees: 2559 Arabic Hadees: 543"
"2560","Al-Silsila-tu-Ahadees-e-Sahiha Hadees: 2560 Arabic Hadees: 2669"
"2561","Al-Silsila-tu-Ahadees-e-Sahiha Hadees: 2561 Arabic Hadees: 2291"
"2562","Al-Silsila-tu-Ahadees-e-Sahiha Hadees: 2562 Arabic Hadees: 3364"
"2563","Al-Silsila-tu-Ahadees-e-Sahiha Hadees: 2563 Arabic Hadees: 3371"
"2564","Al-Silsila-tu-Ahadees-e-Sahiha Hadees: 2564 Arabic Hadees: 3073"
"2565","On the authority of Abu Hurayrah, attributed to the Prophet: Verily, Gog and Magog dig every day until, when they almost see the rays of the sun, the one in charge of them says: ""Return, for we will dig it tomorrow."" Then Allah restores it stronger than before. This continues until their appointed term arrives and Allah wills to send them against the people. They dig until, when they almost see the rays of the sun, the one in charge of them says: ""Return, for we will dig it tomorrow, if Allah wills,"" and they make the exception. So they return to it and find it as they left it. They then dig through it and emerge upon the people. They drink up the waters, and the people take refuge in their fortresses. They shoot their arrows into the sky, and the arrows return stained with clotted blood. They say: ""We have conquered the people of earth and prevailed over the people of heaven."" Then Allah sends a worm (or insect) into their necks, and they are killed by it. The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, the beasts of the earth will grow fat and give thanks from their flesh."""
"2566","Al-Silsila-tu-Ahadees-e-Sahiha Hadees: 2566 Arabic Hadees: 935"
"2567","Junadah ibn Abi Umayyah al-Dawsi said: I and a companion of mine entered upon a man from the Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. We said: ""Narrate to us what you heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and do not narrate to us from anyone other than him, even if he is trustworthy in our view."" He said: ""Yes. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood among us one day and said: 'I warn you of the Dajjal, I warn you of the Dajjal, I warn you of the Dajjal. For there has been no prophet but he warned his nation of him. And he is among you, O nation. And he is curly-haired, dark-skinned, with his left eye obliterated (blind). And with him are a Paradise and a Fire; his Fire is a Paradise and his Paradise is a Fire. And with him are a river of water and a mountain of bread. And he will be empowered over a person, so he will kill him, then bring him back to life; he will not be empowered over anyone else. And he will command the sky to rain, and it will rain, and the earth to bring forth vegetation, but it will not bring forth. And he will remain on the earth for forty mornings, until he reaches every watering place (or pass) of it. And he will not approach four mosques: the Sacred Mosque, the Mosque of the Messenger, the Mosque of Jerusalem, and Mount Tur. And whatever of things becomes ambiguous to you, then verily Allah is not one-eyed (repeated twice).'"""
"2568","Al-Silsila-tu-Ahadees-e-Sahiha Hadees: 2568 Arabic Hadees: 936"
"2569","Al-Silsila-tu-Ahadees-e-Sahiha Hadees: 2569 Arabic Hadees: 3096"
"2570","Al-Silsila-tu-Ahadees-e-Sahiha Hadees: 2570 Arabic Hadees: 3211"
"2571","Al-Silsila-tu-Ahadees-e-Sahiha Hadees: 2571 Arabic Hadees: 3248"
"2572","On the authority of Abdullah ibn Rafi', the freed slave of Umm Salamah, from Umm Salamah, the wife of the Prophet (peace be upon him), that she said: ""I used to hear the people mentioning the Pool (Al-Hawd), but I did not hear that from the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him). Then, one day, while a servant girl was combing my hair, I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) saying: 'O people!' I said to the servant girl: 'Move away from me.' She said: 'He only called the men; he did not call the women.' I said: 'I am among the people.' The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: 'I am your precursor at the Pool, so beware! Let none of you come to me and be driven away from me as a stray camel is driven away, so that I say: ""What is the matter with this?"" And it is said: ""You do not know what they innovated after you."" So I say: ""Away with them! Away with them!""'"""
"2573","On the authority of Ibn ʿAbbās, from ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ""I am holding you back from the Fire by your waist-wrappers, yet you rush into it like moths and locusts. Soon I shall let go of your waist-wrappers, and I shall be your predecessor at the Basin; you will come to me in groups and scattered, and I shall recognize you by your names and your marks, just as a man recognizes his stray camel among his camels. Then a group will be driven to the left, and I shall plead for you to the Lord of the Worlds, saying: 'O Lord, my Ummah!' It will be said: 'You do not know what they innovated after you; they kept turning back on their heels after you.' So I shall not recognize any of you who comes on the Day of Resurrection carrying a sheep bleating, calling: 'O Muḥammad! O Muḥammad!' I shall say: 'I cannot avail you anything against Allah; I have conveyed the message.' And I shall not recognize any of you who comes on the Day of Resurrection carrying a camel grunting, calling: 'O Muḥammad! O Muḥammad!' I shall say: 'I cannot avail you anything against Allah; I have conveyed.' And I shall not recognize any of you who comes on the Day of Resurrection carrying a horse neighing, calling: 'O Muḥammad! O Muḥammad!' I shall say: 'I cannot avail you anything against Allah; I have conveyed.' And I shall not recognize any of you who comes on the Day of Resurrection carrying a piece of leather, calling: 'O Muḥammad! O Muḥammad!' I shall say: 'I cannot avail you anything against Allah; I have conveyed.'"""
"2574","Al-Silsila-tu-Ahadees-e-Sahiha Hadees: 2574 Arabic Hadees: 3180"
"2575","Al-Silsila-tu-Ahadees-e-Sahiha Hadees: 2575 Arabic Hadees: 3386"
