"2578","Al-Silsila-tu-Ahadees-e-Sahiha Hadees: 2578 Arabic Hadees: 3197"
"2579","Al-Silsila-tu-Ahadees-e-Sahiha Hadees: 2579 Arabic Hadees: 2636"
"2580","Al-Silsila-tu-Ahadees-e-Sahiha Hadees: 2580 Arabic Hadees: 3277"
"2581","From ʿAlim, who said: I was with ʿAbis al-Ghifārī on a roof when he saw some people fleeing from the plague. He said: ""What is with these people fleeing from the plague?! O plague! Take me to you (twice)."" His cousin, a Companion, said to him: ""Why do you wish for death when I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'Let none of you wish for death, for when he dies his deeds come to an end, (and he is not returned to make amends).'"" He said: ""Hasten to perform deeds before six characteristics appear: the rule of fools, the abundance of police, the severing of family ties, the selling of judgments, the taking of blood lightly, and a people who take the Quran as psalms, putting forward a man who is not the most knowledgeable among them nor the most learned; they put him forward only to sing for them."""
"2582","Al-Silsila-tu-Ahadees-e-Sahiha Hadees: 2582 Arabic Hadees: 3599"
"2583","Al-Silsila-tu-Ahadees-e-Sahiha Hadees: 2583 Arabic Hadees: 2714"
