"2591","Al-Silsila-tu-Ahadees-e-Sahiha Hadees: 2591 Arabic Hadees: 3125"
"2592","Al-Silsila-tu-Ahadees-e-Sahiha Hadees: 2592 Arabic Hadees: 3178"
"2593","Al-Silsila-tu-Ahadees-e-Sahiha Hadees: 2593 Arabic Hadees: 906"
"2594","Al-Silsila-tu-Ahadees-e-Sahiha Hadees: 2594 Arabic Hadees: 72"
"2595","Al-Silsila-tu-Ahadees-e-Sahiha Hadees: 2595 Arabic Hadees: 726"
"2596","Al-Silsila-tu-Ahadees-e-Sahiha Hadees: 2596 Arabic Hadees: 1186"
"2597","Al-Silsila-tu-Ahadees-e-Sahiha Hadees: 2597 Arabic Hadees: 4034"
"2598","Al-Silsila-tu-Ahadees-e-Sahiha Hadees: 2598 Arabic Hadees: 1170"
"2599","On the authority of ʿAmr ibn Wābiṣah al-Asadī from his father, who said: I was in Kufa in my house when I heard at the door of the house: ""Peace be upon you, may I enter?"" I said: ""And upon you be peace, enter."" When he entered, it was ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd. I said: ""O Abū ʿAbdur-Raḥmān! What hour of visitation is this?"" And that was at the height of midday. He said: ""The day became long for me, so I remembered whom I could converse with."" He said: So he began narrating to me about the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and I narrated to him. Then he began narrating to me. He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: ""There will be a tribulation in which the sleeper is better than the one lying down, and the one lying down is better than the one sitting, and the one sitting is better than the one standing, and the one standing is better than the one walking, and the one walking is better than the one riding, and the one riding is better than the one running. All its killed ones are in the Fire."" I said: ""O Messenger of Allah! And when is that?"" He said: ""That is during the days of Harj (killing/chaos)."" I said: ""And when are the days of Harj?"" He said: ""When a man does not feel safe from his companion."" I said: ""What do you command me if I reach that time?"" He said: ""Restrain yourself and your hand, and enter your house."" I said: ""O Messenger of Allah! What if someone enters upon me in my house?"" He said: ""Then enter your room."" I said: ""O Messenger of Allah! What if someone enters upon me in my room?"" He said: ""Then enter your mosque, and do thus""—and he grasped his right hand on his elbow—""and say: My Lord is Allah, until you die upon that."""
"2600","From Subay', who said: They sent me from Ma' to Kufa to purchase mounts. We came to the Kunasa (market), and there was a man surrounded by a crowd. My companion went to the mounts, while I approached him and found it was Hudhayfa. I heard him saying: ""The Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to ask him about good, but I used to ask him about evil. I said: 'O Messenger of Allah, will there be evil after this good, just as there was evil before it?' He said: 'Yes.' I said: 'Then what is the protection from it?' He said: 'The sword, I think.' I said: 'Then what?' He said: 'Then there will be a truce on a dubious basis (dakhan), then there will be callers to misguidance.' He said: 'If you see on that day the Caliph of Allah on earth, then cling to him, even if he exhausts your body and takes your wealth. If you do not see him, then flee in the earth, even if you die while clinging to the root of a tree.' I said: 'Then what?' He said: 'Then the Dajjal will emerge...' — the hadith continues."
"2601","Al-Silsila-tu-Ahadees-e-Sahiha Hadees: 2601 Arabic Hadees: 818"
"2602","Al-Silsila-tu-Ahadees-e-Sahiha Hadees: 2602 Arabic Hadees: 817"
"2603","Al-Silsila-tu-Ahadees-e-Sahiha Hadees: 2603 Arabic Hadees: 3474"
"2604","Al-Silsila-tu-Ahadees-e-Sahiha Hadees: 2604 Arabic Hadees: 2957"
"2605","Al-Silsila-tu-Ahadees-e-Sahiha Hadees: 2605 Arabic Hadees: 2878"
"2606","Al-Silsila-tu-Ahadees-e-Sahiha Hadees: 2606 Arabic Hadees: 915"
"2607","Al-Silsila-tu-Ahadees-e-Sahiha Hadees: 2607 Arabic Hadees: 1189"
"2608","Al-Silsila-tu-Ahadees-e-Sahiha Hadees: 2608 Arabic Hadees: 1205"
"2609","Al-Silsila-tu-Ahadees-e-Sahiha Hadees: 2609 Arabic Hadees: 417"
"2610","Al-Silsila-tu-Ahadees-e-Sahiha Hadees: 2610 Arabic Hadees: 797"
"2611","Al-Silsila-tu-Ahadees-e-Sahiha Hadees: 2611 Arabic Hadees: 418"
"2612","From Anas: That Abdullah ibn Salam came to the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) upon his arrival in Medina and said: ""O Messenger of Allah! I am going to ask you about three things which none knows except a Prophet."" He said: ""Ask."" He said: ""What is the first of the signs of the Hour? And what is the first thing that the people of Paradise will eat? And from where does the child resemble his father and his mother?"" The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""Gabriel has just informed me of them."" He said: ""That is the enemy of the Jews among the angels!"" He said: ""As for the first of the signs of the Hour, it is a fire that will emerge from the East and gather the people to the West. And as for the first thing that the people of Paradise will eat, it is the extra lobe of the fish's liver. And as for the resemblance of the child to his father and mother: if the man's fluid precedes the woman's fluid, the child will resemble him, and if the woman's fluid precedes the man's fluid, the child will resemble her."" He said: ""I bear witness that there is no god but Allah and that you are the Messenger of Allah."" And he said: ""O Messenger of Allah! The Jews are a people of falsehood, and if they learn of my Islam before you ask them about me, they will slander me to you. So send for them and ask them about me: what kind of man is Abdullah ibn Salam among you?"" So he sent for them and said: ""What kind of man is Abdullah ibn Salam among you?"" They said: ""He is our best and the son of our best, our scholar and the son of our scholar, and the most knowledgeable among us."" He said: ""What do you think if he were to become Muslim, would you become Muslim?"" They said: ""May Allah protect him from that!"" Then Ibn Salam came out and said: ""I bear witness that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah."" They said: ""He is our worst and the son of our worst, our ignorant one and the son of our ignorant one."" So he said: ""Ibn Salam, this is what I feared from them."""
"2613","Al-Silsila-tu-Ahadees-e-Sahiha Hadees: 2613 Arabic Hadees: 601"
"2614","Al-Silsila-tu-Ahadees-e-Sahiha Hadees: 2614 Arabic Hadees: 2614"
